# The kerberos extra of the Atlas provider, for the license check only (it is not in the image):
# its requirement, as written in providers/atlas/pyproject.toml (tests/test_locks.py checks it),
# with the dependencies of the image, at the same versions. gssapi and krb5 publish no Linux
# wheel: they are built from their sdists, whose hashes are checked, against the system's MIT
# Kerberos (libkrb5-dev, which Dependabot's image has too). The -r line makes the image lock
# compile first.
-r image.in
-c image.txt
pyspnego[kerberos]>=0.11,<1
